    "text": "In the WorldLines framework, translation of long-term memory into embodied plans is explicitly presented as a solution component, not as a standalone problem definition.",
    "topic": "Role of translation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Partial observability and overwritten world states are cited as environmental preconditions that motivate the need for the translation mechanism.",
    "topic": "Preconditions as motivation"
  },
  {
    "text": "These two descriptions are compatible: the translation is a mechanism that addresses the preconditions, and the framework treats the preconditions as the motivation for that mechanism.",
    "topic": "Compatibility of statements"
  }
]
